Track NOMMU memory-locking contracts on selected flat-RAM targets.

RAM is already resident, but mlock still requires range validation,
per-process state, limits, future-map enforcement and MS_INVALIDATE
exclusion. A lazy low-RAM PFN bitmap avoids VMA splits for partial locks
and file-backed mappings; all state is protected by mmap_lock. Overlapping
locks are idempotent and unmap/exec clear accounting. Reject oversized
future mappings before invoking file callbacks, and unwind reused regions
without dropping another process's reference on late failures.

Resize the VMA lookup tree, file interval tree and total_vm alongside
NOMMU mremap. Preallocate the one tree update before charging locks, so
failure preserves both the old mapping and its accounting.

